# A1/A1.2/A1_11_more_about_yourself.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L2 a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 2)
# Gender markers (m)/(f)/(n) stripped; (formal)/(informal) qualifiers stripped.
# Words already taught in A1.01-A1.09 (al, d'Stad, kënnen, wunnen, fueren,
# schaffen, schwätzen) are reused in sentences below but not re-declared here.

@lesson A1.11 "More About Yourself"

# --- Age, marital & relationship status ---
@word den Alter = the age
@word jonk = young
@word bestuet = married
@word Single = single

# --- Places ---
@word de Wunnuert = the place of residence
@word den Aarbechtsuert = the work place
@word d'Land = the country
@word de Bierg = the mountain
@word d'Belsch = Belgium
@word Lëtzebuerg = Luxembourg
@word Däitschland = Germany
@word Berlin = Berlin
@word Sandweiler = Sandweiler

# --- Languages ---
@word Franséisch = French
@word Däitsch = German
@word fléissend = fluently

# --- Professions ---
@word de Beruff = the profession
@word den Dokter = the doctor
@word d'Doktesch = the doctor
@word de Proff = the secondary school teacher
@word de Schoulmeeschter = the primary school teacher
@word d'Schouljoffer = the primary school teacher (female)

# --- Family & pets ---
@word d'Duechter = the daughter
@word d'Duechteren = the daughters
@word d'Kaz = the cat
@word d'Kazen = the cats
@word de Mupp = the pooch
@word d'Muppen = the pooches

# --- Other useful words ---
@word keng = no, none
@word mee = but
@word laang = long
@word doheem = at home
@word geschwënn = soon
@word buschtawéieren = to spell

@sentence
@lu Ech si jonk.
@en I am young.
@distractor-en old
@distractor-en married
@distractor-lu al
@distractor-lu bestuet

@sentence
@lu Hien ass al.
@en He is old.
@distractor-en young
@distractor-en married
@distractor-lu jonk
@distractor-lu bestuet

@sentence
